{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c55b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2e-304f-7791-b344-a738da145935"},"sequence":264,"recorded_at":1780531400000523,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3f9b309c-9633-41a9-b30f-c2d9c31c28f3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3f9b309c-9633-41a9-b30f-c2d9c31c28f3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3f9b309c-9633-41a9-b30f-c2d9c31c28f3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae2e-c03c-7b90-ab67-6c4ade9bb7df"},"task_id":"01a0ae2e-c03c-7b90-ab67-6c4ade9bb7df","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae2e-c03c-7b90-ab67-6c4ade9bb7df","chunk":"Read text file `internal/sessrepo/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2f5393: implementation evidence\n2|\n3|Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec v0.6.0, commit\n4|`0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6`. Primary scope is Sections\n5|2.2, 5.3, and 13.6-13.10 (lease creation, renewal, expiry policy, epoch\n6|monotonicity, holder identity, compare-and-swap writes). Historical\n7|scope is retained without weakening: v0.5.0 (commit\n8|`28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c`), Sections 2.3, 5.1-5.2,\n9|5.7, 14.4. This file records implementation evidence; it changes no\n10|normative ownership and claims no public CLI delivery.\n11|\n12|The lease store (`lease_store.go`) extends this package with the durable\n13|Lease Record 1.0.0 lifecycle. It mints no second lease model: closed\n14|shape, self identity, and the three Section 5.3 couplings stay owned by\n15|`canonicaljson`; the winning-tuple rule stays owned by `sessstate`\n16|(`CompareLeaseTuple` restates it because `sessstate` imports this\n17|package, and a cross-package agreement test pins identical order); and\n18|query-layer admission (`sessquery` `winningLeaseFor`) is unchanged — an\n19|adoption test proves store-minted records admit there with the same\n20|digest, epoch, lease ID, and holder.\n21|\n22|## Acceptance rows\n23|\n24|8 of 8 AC rows are driven at the production entries named below; 0 of 8\n25|are delivered as a public CLI surface, which is an explicit\n26|caller-integration bound (no `ax` session command exists in this tree),\n27|not a gap in the assigned shared behavior. Takeover/fork/stop/resume\n28|orchestration, checkpoint admission, and cross-partition union\n29|convergence belong to their owning leaves, which invoke this API at\n30|every required boundary.\n31|\n32|| AC row | Production call site | Named test(s) | Evidence and bound |\n33|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n34|| Lease creation | `Repository.CreateLease` | `TestCreateLeasePersistsEpochOneCreate`, `TestCreateLeaseRequiresExistingSession`, `TestCreateLeaseRefusesInvalidIdentity`, `TestCreateLeaseIsIdempotentOnByteIdenticalRetry`, `TestCreateLeaseRefusesSecondCreateWithDifferingBytes`, `TestNormativeLeaseRecordExampleAttests` | Driven: epoch-1 `create` minted from the durable bootstrap inputs (existing session record plus caller fencing token, holder, issuer, timestamp), attested through the canonical owner with null predecessor/checkpoint; unknown session refuses; malformed members refuse `invalid lease record`; byte-identical retry replays the same reference; a differing second create refuses `lease already exists` with the persisted lease undisturbed. The verbatim Section 5.3 example attests to its pinned digest. |\n35|| Renewal | `Repository.VerifyFencingToken` | `TestVerifyFencingTokenAcceptsWinner`, `TestVerifyFencingTokenRefusals` | Driven: a token matching the winning tuple and holder revalidates (nil); epoch 0, malformed lease/holder refuse `invalid lease record`; a superseded epoch refuses `stale lease epoch`; a beyond-head epoch (including any token on an empty store) refuses `unknown lease`; a same-epoch foreign lease refuses `lease_conflict`; a foreign holder refuses `lease_holder_mismatch`. Renewal mints no lease and mutates no durable state. |\n36|| Expiry policy | `CheckFencingExpiry`; `Repository.VerifyFencingToken` + `Repository.WinningLease` | `TestCheckFencingExpiry`, `TestLeaseNeverExpiresWithAge` | Driven: a grant older than the refresh interval refuses `fencing_grant_expired` with revalidation as the remedy; a grant at exactly the boundary stays current; a non-positive interval refuses `invalid lease record`. The lease itself never expires: an ancient `created_at` still verifies and still wins (Section 5.3 \"no time-expiring ownership lease\"; liveness is not authority). Grants are process-local and never persisted. |\n37|| Epoch monotonicity | `Repository.CompareAndSwapLease` → head+1 derivation; `Repository.ListLeases` order | `TestCompareAndSwapPersistsSuccessor`, `TestEpochMonotonicityAcrossSuccessors`, `TestCompareAndSwapIsIdempotentOnByteIdenticalRetry` | Driven: every successor lands at exactly head epoch plus one with the head fencing token as predecessor — the epoch is never taken from input, so it can neither skip nor decrease; three successions pin epochs 2-4 with a linked predecessor chain; list order is ascending tuple order. A superseded expectation refuses stale (or replays the persisted successor on a byte-identical retry). Epoch gaps and cycles cannot be minted here; out-of-band ones still refuse at query admission. |\n38|| Holder identity | `Repository.CreateLease`, `Repository.CompareAndSwapLease`, `Repository.VerifyFencingToken` | Holder arms of `TestCreateLeaseRefusesInvalidIdentity`, `TestCompareAndSwapRefusesInvalidSuccessor`, `TestVerifyFencingTokenRefusals` (`holder mismatch`), `TestCompareAndSwapPersistsSuccessor` | Driven: holder and issuer must be UUIDv7 host identities; the successor binds its holder; a token from a non-holder refuses `lease_holder_mismatch`. Process binding is machine-local and never persisted cross-host (Section 2.2 invariants 4-5). |\n39|| Compare-and-swap writes | `Repository.CompareAndSwapLease` | `TestCompareAndSwapPersistsSuccessor`, `TestCompareAndSwapRequiresExistingLease`, `TestCompareAndSwapRefusesInvalidSuccessor`, `TestCompareAndSwapRefusesFencingTokenReuse`, `TestCompareAndSwapRefusesStaleExpectation`, `TestCompareAndSwapRefusesUnknownExpectation`, `TestCompareAndSwapIsIdempotentOnByteIdenticalRetry` | Driven: an expectation naming the head persists the successor; an expectation naming nothing known (malformed, empty, foreign) refuses `lease_conflict`; a superseded expectation refuses `stale lease epoch`; CAS on an empty store refuses `unknown lease`; a reused fencing token refuses `invalid lease record`; a non-enum reason or absent/malformed checkpoint refuses `invalid lease record`; a byte-identical retry re-mints against its pre-commit basis and replays the persisted successor. Full checkpoint-record admission stays with the query layer (stated bound). |\n40|| Contract fixtures and negative/refusal cases | All gates below; `AttestLeaseRecord` | Every `Test*` arm above plus `TestStoredLeaseCorruptionRefuses`, `TestInstallDisagreeingBytesRefuses`, `TestGetLeaseRefusals`, `TestWinningLeaseRefusesEmptyStore`, `TestLeaseStageTempsAreIgnored`, `TestLeaseTupleOrderAgreesWithSessstateCompare`, `TestLeaseStoreRecordsAdmitWithoutBehavioralChange` | Driven: the normative example attests; torn blobs (unparseable names, undecodable/truncated bytes, cross-session plants, digest-name disagreement) refuse chain corruption through both funnels; disagreeing bytes at install refuse (same- and different-length arms); malformed/unknown reads refuse their classes; orphaned stage temps are ignored; the tuple rule agrees with `sessstate.Compare` on a pinned corpus; store-minted records admit through unchanged `winningLeaseFor`/`BuildPlan`/`Revalidate`. |\n41|| Crash/idempotency evidence | `Repository.CreateLease`, `Repository.CompareAndSwapLease` + `BeforeWrite`/`AfterCommit`/`AfterLeaseStage` | `TestCrashBeforeLeaseWriteIsSafeRetry`, `TestCrashAfterLeaseCommitCountsAsCommitted`, `TestLeaseKillAtRenameSeam/create`, `TestLeaseKillAtRenameSeam/cas` | Driven: an injected pre-write fault carries `safe_retry` with nothing mutated and the retry succeeding; an injected post-commit fault carries `recoverable_parked_state` with the commit durable and the byte-identical retry replaying the same reference. A real SIGKILLed child at the stage-then-rename seam leaves no torn final (create: zero finals plus one ignored temp; CAS: the prior final plus one ignored temp); a fresh handle reopens cleanly and the byte-identical retry lands the exact epoch. See the recovery table below. |\n42|\n43|## Refusal and recovery coverage\n44|\n45|Every `N-` row is a genuine narrowing mutant: the gate stays present\n46|and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must\n47|reject, and the named behavioral test fails through the delivered\n48|harness (`internal/sessrepo/testdata/mutate.py`, run as\n49|`python3 internal/sessrepo/testdata/mutate.py <evidence-dir>`).\n50|Whole-clause disables are not accepted as narrowing. The `T-` row\n51|preserves the searched-for timestamp token while changing behavior.\n52|Controls are reported separately and never counted as kills.\n53|\n54|Final battery (`mutants-03`, on the exact final source): 26 narrowing\n55|(one per `refuse` site) + 1 token-preserving, all `KILLED`; the applied\n56|harmless control is `SURVIVED`, while the not-applied and\n57|compile-failure controls are classified separately. Battery exit 0.\n58|\n59|| Gate | Real entry test | Narrowing attack (all killed) |\n60|| --- | --- | --- |\n61|| Create fencing-token grammar | `TestCreateLeaseRefusesInvalidIdentity/lease_token` | N-create-token admits exactly `not-a-uuid`; mint then fails closed with a plain error and the refusal class changes. |\n62|| Create holder grammar | `TestCreateLeaseRefusesInvalidIdentity/holder` | N-create-holder admits exactly `not-a-uuid`; same closed mint failure. |\n63|| Create issuer grammar | `TestCreateLeaseRefusesInvalidIdentity/issuer` | N-create-issuer admits exactly the Q-suffixed issuer; same closed mint failure. |\n64|| Create timestamp grammar | `TestCreateLeaseRefusesInvalidIdentity/created_at`, `/created_at_padded` | N-create-time admits exactly `not-a-timestamp` (mint succeeds: no downstream check); T-create-time-pad parses the same token whitespace-tolerantly and admits the padded value. |\n65|| Successor reason enum | `TestCompareAndSwapRefusesInvalidSuccessor/reason` | N-successor-reason admits exactly `bogus_reason`; mint fails closed and the refusal class changes. |\n66|| Successor checkpoint grammar | `TestCompareAndSwapRefusesInvalidSuccessor/checkpoint_malformed` | N-successor-checkpoint admits exactly `not-a-digest`; absent and other malformed values still refuse. |\n67|| Create-once | `TestCreateLeaseRefusesSecondCreateWithDifferingBytes` | N-create-once admits exactly a depth-one second create; a third create past a succession still refuses. |\n68|| Fencing-token uniqueness | `TestCompareAndSwapRefusesFencingTokenReuse` | N-cas-token-reuse admits exactly the epoch-1 token reuse; the CAS succeeds and the negative fails. |\n69|| CAS conflict | `TestCompareAndSwapRefusesUnknownExpectation/foreign` | N-cas-conflict admits exactly the foreign digest; replay minting fails closed and the refusal class changes. |\n70|| CAS stale basis | `TestCompareAndSwapRefusesStaleExpectation` | N-cas-stale admits exactly epoch-1 stale bases; the epoch-2 arm still refuses. |\n71|| CAS empty store | `TestCompareAndSwapRequiresExistingLease` | N-cas-empty admits exactly the empty-expectation CAS; a named expectation on an empty store still refuses. |\n72|| Fencing token grammar (epoch/lease/holder) | `TestVerifyFencingTokenRefusals/epoch_zero`, `/lease_malformed`, `/holder_malformed` | N-fence-token-epoch/lease/holder admit exactly the suite vectors; each refusal degrades to its downstream class (stale/conflict/mismatch). |\n73|| Fencing stale epoch | `TestVerifyFencingTokenRefusals/stale_epoch` | N-fence-stale admits exactly the epoch-1 token; the refusal degrades to conflict. |\n74|| Fencing future epoch | `TestVerifyFencingTokenRefusals/future_epoch` | N-fence-future admits exactly epoch 9; the empty-store epoch-1 token still refuses unknown. |\n75|| Fencing same-epoch tie | `TestVerifyFencingTokenRefusals/losing_lease` | N-fence-loser admits exactly the leaseC loser; the token verifies and the negative fails by success. |\n76|| Fencing holder binding | `TestVerifyFencingTokenRefusals/holder_mismatch` | N-fence-holder admits exactly the hostA non-holder; the token verifies and the negative fails by success. |\n77|| Grant-expiry policy shape | `TestCheckFencingExpiry` | N-expiry-policy admits exactly the zero interval; a negative interval still refuses. |\n78|| Grant-expiry lapse | `TestCheckFencingExpiry` | N-expiry-lapsed admits exactly the suite lapsed grant; the grant verifies and the negative fails by success. |\n79|| Lease load funnel | `TestStoredLeaseCorruptionRefuses/unparseable_name` | N-load-funnel admits exactly the garbage-name vector; truncated, cross-session, misnamed, and undecodable vectors still refuse. |\n80|| GetLease funnel | `TestStoredLeaseCorruptionRefuses/undecodable_bytes` | N-get-funnel admits exactly the undecodable vector; the misnamed vector still refuses. |\n81|| Install content equality | `TestInstallDisagreeingBytesRefuses/same_length` | N-install-length compares length only at the ledgered site; the same-length garbage arm reuses while the different-length arm still refuses. |\n82|| GetLease malformed reference | `TestGetLeaseRefusals` | N-get-malformed admits exactly `not-a-digest`; the refusal degrades to unknown. |\n83|| GetLease unknown reference | `TestGetLeaseRefusals` | N-get-unknown admits exactly the foreign digest; the refusal degrades to corruption. |\n84|| Winning-lease absence | `TestWinningLeaseRefusesEmptyStore` | N-winning-empty admits exactly the suite empty store with a zero summary; the negative fails by success. |\n85|\n86|Crash/idempotency matrix (Section 13.13 outcomes):\n87|\n88|| Boundary | Required recovery | Evidence |\n89|| --- | --- | --- |\n90|| Before first lease byte (`CR-MAT-prepare-enter`) | `safe_retry`: nothing mutated, identical retry succeeds | Injector arms on create and CAS; kill drill shows zero premature finals. |\n91|| After staged fsync, before rename (`AfterLeaseStage`) | `safe_retry`: only an orphaned ignored temp, identical retry lands the exact epoch | Real SIGKILL child drills for create and CAS with fresh-handle reopen and temp-tolerance assertions. |\n92|| After install (`CR-MAT-commit-apply`) | Committed: the lease reads back, the byte-identical retry replays the same reference (CAS re-mints against its pre-commit basis) | Injector arms on create and CAS. |\n93|| Disagreeing bytes at a digest path | Torn store: no retry heals; operator removes the session directory | Same- and different-length plant arms; post-plant reads funnel chain corruption. |\n94|\n95|## Bounds (not silent gaps)\n96|\n97|- No public CLI: 0 of 8 rows are delivered as an `ax` command. The\n98|  shared-library entries above are the deliverable; orchestration leaves\n99|  invoke them.\n100|- No checkpoint admission on the write path: CAS requires a well-formed\n101|  checkpoint digest, but validating the referenced Checkpoint Record\n102|  stays with `sessquery` admission.\n103|- No cross-partition union convergence: same-epoch concurrent leases\n104|  from partitioned writers reconcile in the sibling ownership leaves;\n105|  this store orders whatever blobs exist by the shared tuple rule.\n106|- No wall-clock lease expiry and no persisted grants: expiry retires\n107|  only the process-local authorization; the lease stays authoritative.\n108|- Mint failures are plain operational errors, never refusals: entry\n109|  validation already admitted the inputs, so a mint failure is an\n110|  internal inconsistency. The narrowing batteries rely on this: a\n111|  weakened grammar gate fails closed at mint with a changed class.","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c55d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2e-304f-7791-b344-a738da145935"},"sequence":265,"recorded_at":1780531400000525,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3f9b309c-9633-41a9-b30f-c2d9c31c28f3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3f9b309c-9633-41a9-b30f-c2d9c31c28f3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3f9b309c-9633-41a9-b30f-c2d9c31c28f3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae2e-c03c-7b90-ab67-6c4ade9bb7df"},"task_id":"01a0ae2e-c03c-7b90-ab67-6c4ade9bb7df","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0ae2e-c03c-7b90-ab67-6c4ade9bb7df"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c55f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2e-304f-7791-b344-a738da145935"},"sequence":266,"recorded_at":1780531400000527,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3f9b309c-9633-41a9-b30f-c2d9c31c28f3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3f9b309c-9633-41a9-b30f-c2d9c31c28f3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3f9b309c-9633-41a9-b30f-c2d9c31c28f3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae2e-bff1-7ae3-b324-816f36acdc00"},"task_id":"01a0ae2e-bff1-7ae3-b324-816f36acdc00","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae2e-bff1-7ae3-b324-816f36acdc00","chunk":"Read text file `internal/sessrepo/doc.go`.\n1|// Package sessrepo persists and validates AX Session Records, the\n2|// append-only per-session event chain with source sequence continuity, and\n3|// the Lease Record lifecycle with compare-and-swap succession.\n4|//\n5|// Normative scope: AX v0.5.0 sections 2.3 (session name resolution), 5.1\n6|// (Session Record), 5.2 (Session Event), 5.7 (derived session states), and\n7|// 14.4 (list and status fields), plus the v0.6.0 lease lifecycle in\n8|// sections 2.2 (global invariants), 5.3 (Lease Record and ownership), and\n9|// 13.6-13.10 (takeover, fork, stop, resume). This package owns durable\n10|// session state: the immutable record, the ordered event chain beneath it,\n11|// the immutable lease blobs with their winning head, and the stored\n12|// identity fields that later leaves project into lifecycle state, resolved\n13|// names, and list/status rows.\n14|//\n15|// Division of authority inside this story:\n16|//\n17|//   - Validation of record, event, and lease closed shapes and of every\n18|//     self-identity digest is owned by internal/canonicaljson and reached\n19|//     only through its production entries (VerifyObjectIdentity for\n20|//     attestation, CalculateObjectIdentity for minting identity). Entry\n21|//     decodes refuse a foreign schema before Verify; the load path\n22|//     re-verifies stored blobs through Verify — recomputing whatever\n23|//     digest the bytes claim — and refuses a non-event_id self field or\n24|//     an index-disagreeing digest at its named arms, or a torn lease blob\n25|//     through the lease load funnel. This package never re-decodes a\n26|//     frame, never recomputes a bound, and never selects a self field.\n27|//   - Strict frame decoding and scalar bound checks on the members this\n28|//     package must read (session and lease identifiers, lease_sequence,\n29|//     predecessor digests, names, fencing tokens, timestamps) are owned by\n30|//     internal/environ and internal/scalar and reached only through their\n31|//     production checks.\n32|//   - Crash-point vocabulary and outcomes are owned by\n33|//     internal/secconftest. The repository fires the owner's own points\n34|//     through the owner's Injector: a fault before the durable write carries\n35|//     safe_retry, a fault after it carries recoverable_parked_state, and a\n36|//     crashed commit counts as committed.\n37|//   - The refusal census denominator is derived from production through\n38|//     internal/invcore; see census_test.go.\n39|//   - The winning-tuple rule is owned by internal/sessstate (Compare).\n40|//     The lease store restates it as CompareLeaseTuple because sessstate\n41|//     imports this package, and a cross-package agreement test pins\n42|//     identical order. Query-layer admission (internal/sessquery\n43|//     winningLeaseFor) is unchanged and admits store-minted records.\n44|//\n45|// Per-session parked reporting (SPEC.md:9082, Section 13.13\n46|// recoverable_parked_state; Section 14.4 per-session warnings).\n47|//\n48|// ListSessions reports one entry per session directory in session-ID\n49|// order. A session whose bytes no longer verify is returned as a parked\n50|// entry — Parked=true with the blocking reason and the same-operation\n51|// retry — and never fails the listing for its healthy siblings. Resolve\n52|// routes only healthy sessions; a query naming only a parked session is\n53|// not found. GetRecord, GetEvent, and ListEvents still refuse a parked\n54|// session per session with the load failure.\n55|//\n56|// Why per-session instead of repository-wide closure: a repository-wide\n57|// listing error carries no per-session channel, so the Section 5.7\n58|// reducer and the Section 14.4 rendering leaves could not project the\n59|// parked lifecycle state, the blocking reason, or the warnings from what\n60|// this leaf exposes — and one torn session denied listing and name\n61|// resolution to every healthy sibling permanently when its original\n62|// bytes were lost. Per-session reporting keeps healthy sessions usable\n63|// while the parked session stays visible. The tradeoff is that callers\n64|// must check Parked: a listing that contains parked entries returns nil\n65|// error by design.\n66|//\n67|// Retry table (same-operation retry, Section 13.13):\n68|//\n69|//   - Bare session directory (no record.json, no chain.json): retry\n70|//     CreateSession with the session record for this session ID. Any\n71|//     valid record for the ID resumes; the parked state is the bare\n72|//     directory left by a crash between the directory and record steps.\n73|//   - Record parked without a chain index (record.json verifies, no\n74|//     chain.json): retry CreateSession with the byte-identical session\n75|//     record. A different record for the same session ID is refused\n76|//     with ErrSessionExists and the parked bytes survive; the\n77|//     byte-equality is full-content, not length-only.\n78|//   - Torn store (chain.json present but the session no longer\n79|//     verifies): no CreateSession retry heals it. A byte-identical\n80|//     retry is refused as an existing session and a differing retry is\n81|//     refused the same way; the store stays parked.\n82|//   - Missing lease after a killed install: retry CreateLease or\n83|//     CompareAndSwapLease with the byte-identical input. The install is\n84|//     stage-then-rename, so a kill leaves at most an orphaned staged\n85|//     temp (ignored on load, never a torn final); the retry replays to\n86|//     the same digest, and a duplicate install of identical bytes is\n87|//     reused. A CAS retry still names its pre-commit expectation: the\n88|//     replay check re-mints against that basis and answers the persisted\n89|//     successor.\n90|//   - Torn lease blob (disagreeing bytes at a digest path, or a blob\n91|//     that no longer attests): no retry heals it. The colliding write is\n92|//     refused with ErrChainCorrupt and every lease read funnels the same\n93|//     class; the operator remedy below applies to the leases namespace.\n94|//\n95|// Operator remedy. There is no delete, prune, or quarantine entry by\n96|// design: records and events are append-only and no production path\n97|// rewrites or deletes an existing entry. When no same-operation retry\n98|// heals a parked session — the original record bytes are lost, or the\n99|// store is torn past the create window — the operator removes the\n100|// session directory at <data-root>/sessions/<session-id> from the\n101|// filesystem after confirming no host will retry with the original\n102|// bytes, and the listing heals on the next read. Removing the directory\n103|// discards whatever that session had parked; it never touches siblings.\n104|// Downstream leaves consume the parked channel as: SessionSummary.Parked\n105|// selects the parked/failed lifecycle projection, BlockingReason feeds\n106|// status/doctor blocking reason and warnings, and RetryHint feeds the\n107|// retry or remedy line.\n108|//\n109|// Stated bounds (not silent gaps):\n110|//\n111|//   - Single authoritative branch. The repository tracks one ordered chain\n112|//     per session in arrival order. A same-epoch event under a different\n113|//     lease is preserved as an immutable blob but refused from the chain\n114|//     with ErrDivergentBranch; converging lease histories across\n115|//     partitions (union and divergent-branch reconciliation) belongs to\n116|//     the sibling ownership leaves, not to this record lifecycle.\n117|//   - No checkpoint admission on the write path. CAS requires a\n118|//     well-formed checkpoint digest for every successor, but validating\n119|//     that the digest names an admitted checkpoint for the predecessor\n120|//     lease stays with the query-layer admission this store feeds.\n121|//   - No wall-clock lease expiry. The lease never expires (Section 5.3);\n122|//     only the process-local fencing grant lapses past the refresh\n123|//     interval, and revalidation renews it. Grants are never persisted\n124|//     and never replicated.\n125|//   - No lifecycle derivation. Section 5.7 SessionState reduction and the\n126|//     full Section 2.3 four-step resolution order (peer-learned names,\n127|//     interactive choice) belong to the sibling reducer and name-resolution\n128|//     leaves. This package exposes the stored facts they project: exact\n129|//     local names with ASCII case-fold ambiguity detection, UUID routing,\n130|//     per-session chain heads, and the parked channel above.\n131|//   - No Section 14.4 rendering. ListSessions exposes stored identity plus\n132|//     chain-head facts (or the parked channel); human or JSON rendering\n133|//     of owner host, checkpoint age, capability status, and warnings\n134|//     belongs to the CLI surface leaf.\n135|//\n136|// The package adds no ax command, no doctor result, and no runtime\n137|// capability claim.\n138|package sessrepo","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c561","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2e-304f-7791-b344-a738da145935"},"sequence":267,"recorded_at":1780531400000529,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3f9b309c-9633-41a9-b30f-c2d9c31c28f3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3f9b309c-9633-41a9-b30f-c2d9c31c28f3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3f9b309c-9633-41a9-b30f-c2d9c31c28f3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae2e-bff1-7ae3-b324-816f36acdc00"},"task_id":"01a0ae2e-bff1-7ae3-b324-816f36acdc00","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0ae2e-bff1-7ae3-b324-816f36acdc00"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c563","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2e-304f-7791-b344-a738da145935"},"sequence":268,"recorded_at":1780531400000531,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3f9b309c-9633-41a9-b30f-c2d9c31c28f3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3f9b309c-9633-41a9-b30f-c2d9c31c28f3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3f9b309c-9633-41a9-b30f-c2d9c31c28f3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae2e-c013-7132-b563-59bd5363c5ca"},"task_id":"01a0ae2e-c013-7132-b563-59bd5363c5ca","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae2e-c013-7132-b563-59bd5363c5ca","chunk":"Read text file `internal/fencing/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-3g12yp: implementation evidence\n2|\n3|Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec v0.6.0, commit\n4|`0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6`. Primary scope is Sections\n5|2.2, 5.3, and 13.6-13.10 (winning lease and exact epoch before\n6|provider activation, input, mutation, checkpoint, or terminal\n7|restore), the Section 4 terminal wrapper rule, and the Section 7.5\n8|`LeaseToken`. This file records implementation evidence; it changes no\n9|normative ownership and claims no public CLI delivery.\n10|\n11|The fencing gates (`internal/fencing`) require the winning lease and\n12|the exact epoch before every activation-class action. They mint no\n13|second lease model: the Lease Record lifecycle stays owned by\n14|`sessrepo` (`Observe` loads the winner through `ListLeases`, the\n15|expiry arm calls `CheckFencingExpiry`); the winning-tuple rule stays\n16|owned by `sessstate` (the gates compare one presented token for exact\n17|equality with the one winning summary and never order two leases);\n18|takeover, fork, stop, and resume transactions, terminal backends, and\n19|provider plugin processes are modeled as callers, not members.\n20|\n21|## Acceptance rows\n22|\n23|18 of 18 AC rows are driven at the production entries named below; 0\n24|of 18 are delivered as a public CLI surface, which is an explicit\n25|caller-integration bound (no `ax` session command exists in this\n26|tree), not a gap in the assigned shared behavior. Takeover/fork/stop/\n27|resume orchestration belongs to its owning leaves, which invoke these\n28|entries at every required boundary.\n29|\n30|| AC row | Production call site | Named test(s) | Evidence and bound |\n31|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n32|| Provider activation requires winner + exact epoch | `AuthorizeActivation` | `TestAuthorizeAdmitsWinnerExactEpochAllOperations`, `TestAuthorizeEndToEndOverRepository`, `TestLifecycleCallersPassTheGate/fork_epoch_one_activation` | Driven: the winning lease with the exact epoch mints through the activation entry over pure and repository-backed observations, including the fork epoch-1 lease; a rival succession parks or refuses the old token. |\n33|| Provider input requires winner + exact epoch | `AuthorizeInput` | `TestAuthorizeAdmitsWinnerExactEpochAllOperations`, `TestOldOwnerReconnectRejectedAfterForceTakeover/new_owner_rejects_old_token_as_stale`, `TestConcurrentForceTakeoversDeterministicWinner` | Driven: exact input authorizes; the old token after a force takeover refuses `stale_owner`; the losing same-epoch token refuses `lease_conflict` once the union winner is known. |\n34|| Owner-authored mutation requires winner + exact epoch | `AuthorizeMutation` | `TestAuthorizeAdmitsWinnerExactEpochAllOperations`, `TestLifecycleCallersPassTheGate/graceful_takeover_commit`, `TestAuthorizeEndToEndOverRepository` | Driven: the modeled graceful-takeover commit authorizes its mutation with the new winning tuple; the source token refuses after the succession. |\n35|| Checkpoint capture requires winner + exact epoch | `AuthorizeCheckpoint` | `TestAuthorizeAdmitsWinnerExactEpochAllOperations`, `TestLifecycleCallersPassTheGate/stop_checkpoint` | Driven: the modeled stop checkpoint authorizes with the exact tuple and refuses `stale_owner` for a superseded token. No second checkpoint admission exists in this tree (the brief's `sessckpt` package is absent), so the gate is the capture admission (stated bound). |\n36|| Terminal restore requires winner + exact epoch | `AuthorizeRestore` | `TestAuthorizeAdmitsWinnerExactEpochAllOperations`, `TestLifecycleCallersPassTheGate/owner_resume_and_replica_park` | Driven: the owner resume authorizes; the replica restore parks `remote_owner` with the `not_owner` cause instead of starting a runtime. |\n37|| Lower epoch refused | `Authorize` via all five entries | `TestAuthorizeRefusesLowerEpoch` | Driven: a superseded epoch refuses `stale_owner` on input/mutation/checkpoint and parks `stale_owner` on activation/restore, for the standard old-lease vector and the winner-lease-at-lower-epoch vector. |\n38|| Same-epoch loser refused | `Authorize` via all five entries | `TestAuthorizeRefusesSameEpochLoser` | Driven: a losing lease at the winning epoch refuses `lease_conflict` on input/mutation/checkpoint and parks `stale_owner` on activation/restore, for the standard and prefix-sharing losers. |\n39|| Foreign session refused | `Authorize` via all five entries | `TestAuthorizeRefusesForeignSession` | Driven: a token for another session refuses `lease_conflict` on every entry, for the prefix-sharing and fully foreign sessions. |\n40|| Expired grant refused | `Authorize` via all five entries → `sessrepo.CheckFencingExpiry` | `TestAuthorizeRefusesExpiredGrant` | Driven: a lapsed grant refuses `lease_conflict` on every entry so the holder revalidates; a grant at exactly the boundary stays current; an unusable policy refuses `invalid_arguments`. Expiry logic is reused from the `sessrepo` owner, never restated. |\n41|| Absent lease parks or refuses | `Authorize` via all five entries; `Observe` | `TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesAbsentWinner`, `TestObserveLoadsWinningLease/no_leases_yields_no_winner` | Driven: with no winning lease, launch entries park `restore_policy` with an empty winning lease ID while the other entries refuse `lease_conflict`; `Observe` reports absence as data, never an error. |\n42|| Ambiguous ownership parks or refuses | `Authorize` via all five entries | `TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesAmbiguous` | Driven: conflicting union observations park `restore_policy` under the winner on launch entries and refuse `lease_conflict` elsewhere. |\n43|| Remote ownership parks or refuses | `Authorize` via all five entries | `TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesRemote` | Driven: a remote winning holder parks `remote_owner` under the winner on launch entries and refuses `not_owner` elsewhere, for prefix-sharing and fully remote holders. |\n44|| Unverified sync parks or refuses | `Authorize` via all five entries | `TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesUnverified` | Driven: without a proving lease refresh, launch entries park `restore_policy` under the winner and the other entries refuse `lease_conflict`. |\n45|| Old-owner reconnect rejected, divergent history preserved | `AuthorizeInput`, `AuthorizeMutation`, `AuthorizeRestore`, `AuthorizeActivation`, `Repository.AppendEvent`, `sessstate.Projector.Project` | `TestOldOwnerReconnectRejectedAfterForceTakeover` | Driven: after a force takeover the old token refuses `stale_owner` from input/mutation/checkpoint on the new owner and parks `remote_owner` on the old wrapper; the losing event refuses stale with its bytes preserved and the chain untouched; the union projection reports `losing_branch_preserved` and `union_supersedes_chain` with authoritative state standing and the old-owner view stale. |\n46|| Concurrent force takeovers resolve deterministically | `sessrepo.CompareLeaseTuple`, `sessstate.Compare`, `AuthorizeInput`, `AuthorizeMutation`, `AuthorizeActivation` | `TestConcurrentForceTakeoversDeterministicWinner` | Driven: two same-epoch force leases from one base resolve to the greater lease ID in either union order under both tuple rules; the winner authorizes and the loser stops accepting input with `lease_conflict`. |\n47|| Token forgery refused | `LeaseToken.Bind`; constructor census | `TestBindRefusesForgedToken`, `TestLeaseTokenConstructorCensus`, `TestLeaseTokenCensusPlants`, `TestLeaseTokenUnforgeableOutsidePackage` | Driven: zero and field-assembled tokens refuse `lease_conflict` on every provider operation; only `token.go` names the seal types or assembles a non-empty token; comment/string mentions are not references while alias, direct, and shadowing forgeries are rejected; an outside package assembling the token by field name fails to build while the public-surface fixture builds. |\n48|| Terminate-stale outside force recovery refused | `AuthorizeTerminateStale` | `TestTerminateStaleAuthorizesFencedTarget`, `TestTerminateStaleRefusesWithoutForce`, `TestTerminateStaleRefusesWithoutDiagnostics`, `TestTerminateStaleRefusesWithoutWinner`, `TestTerminateStaleRefusesLiveOwner`, `TestTerminateStaleRefusesForeignSession`, `TestTerminateStaleRefusesMalformedTarget`, `TestTerminateStaleRefusesGarbageWinner` | Driven: a fenced target (lower epoch, divergent, or beyond the winner) authorizes under explicit force recovery with preserved diagnostics; missing force, diagnostics, or winner, a live-owner target, a foreign session, and malformed members refuse their classes. |\n49|| LeaseToken bound to provider operations from a passed gate only | `LeaseToken.Bind` | `TestBindProjectsMintedToken`, `TestBindRefusesUnknownOperation`, `TestMintedTokenIsStableAcrossEntries` | Driven: a token minted by a passed gate projects the exact triple onto `quiesce`, `capture`, and `materialize` identically from every entry; unknown operations refuse `invalid_arguments`. Resume, stop, materialize-commit, and native-store-plan carry the same triple on the wire but have no gate entry here (stated bound). |\n50|\n51|## Refusal and recovery coverage\n52|\n53|Every `N-` row is a genuine narrowing mutant: the gate stays present\n54|and is weakened to admit exactly one member of the class it must\n55|reject, and the named behavioral test fails through the delivered\n56|harness (`internal/fencing/testdata/mutate.py`, run as\n57|`python3 internal/fencing/testdata/mutate.py <evidence-dir>`).\n58|Whole-clause disables are not accepted as narrowing. The `T-` row\n59|preserves the searched-for `leaseSeal` token while constructing\n60|through an alias, and its harness run executes the full behavioral\n61|suite (263 passing assertions alongside the census failure), not only\n62|the static checker. Controls: `C-harmless-comment` is applied and\n63|survives, `C-not-applied` is not a kill, and `C-compile-failure`\n64|produces no named behavioral failure.\n65|\n66|| Gate | Named test | Narrowing mutant |\n67|| --- | --- | --- |\n68|| Operation enum | `TestAuthorizeRefusesUnknownOperation` | N-op admits exactly the bogus operation; the token authorizes and the negative fails by success. |\n69|| Presented session grammar | `TestAuthorizeRefusesMalformedPresented/session_not_uuid` | N-presented-session admits exactly `not-a-uuid`; the refusal degrades to the foreign-session class. |\n70|| Presented epoch grammar | `TestAuthorizeRefusesMalformedPresented/epoch_zero` | N-presented-epoch admits exactly the epoch-zero winner-lease vector; the refusal degrades to the stale class. |\n71|| Presented lease grammar | `TestAuthorizeRefusesMalformedPresented/lease_not_uuid` | N-presented-lease admits exactly `zzz`; the refusal degrades to the loser class. |\n72|| Winner grammar | `TestAuthorizeRefusesGarbageWinner/epoch_zero_lease` | N-winner admits exactly the epoch-zero `zzz` winner; the refusal degrades to the ahead class. |\n73|| Session binding | `TestAuthorizeRefusesForeignSession/prefix_sharing` | N-session-prefix compares first UUID segments only; the prefix-sharing session authorizes while the fully foreign session still refuses. |\n74|| Winner absence | `TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesAbsentWinner/verified` | N-absent admits exactly the verified absence; the refusal degrades to the malformed-observation class. |\n75|| Sync verification | `TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesUnverified/unambiguous` | N-verified admits exactly the unambiguous unverified observation; the token authorizes and the negative fails by success. |\n76|| Ambiguity | `TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesAmbiguous/verified` | N-ambiguous admits exactly the verified ambiguity; the token authorizes and the negative fails by success. |\n77|| Handoff outcome | `TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesFailedHandoff/verified` | N-handoff admits exactly the verified failed handoff; the token authorizes and the negative fails by success. |\n78|| Grant presence | `TestAuthorizeRefusesMissingGrant/verified` | N-grant admits exactly the verified grantless call; the refusal degrades to the lapsed-grant class. |\n79|| Clock presence | `TestAuthorizeRefusesMissingClock/zero_validated` | N-clock admits exactly the clockless never-validated grant; the token authorizes and the negative fails by success. |\n80|| Grant expiry | `TestAuthorizeRefusesExpiredGrant/lapsed` | N-expiry extends the interval by an hour; the lapsed-by-seconds grant authorizes while the never-validated grant still refuses. |\n81|| Expiry classification | `TestAuthorizeRefusesExpiredGrant` | N-expiry-map swaps the lapsed/unusable classes; both vectors change class. |\n82|| Ownership direction | `TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesRemote/prefix_sharing` | N-remote-prefix compares first UUID segments only; the prefix-sharing remote holder authorizes while the fully remote holder still refuses. |\n83|| Epoch equality, ahead side | `TestAuthorizeRefusesEpochBeyondWinner/exact_lease` | N-epoch-gte weakens `==` to `>=`; the ahead token authorizes while the lower-epoch vectors still refuse stale in the same run. |\n84|| Epoch equality, lower side | `TestAuthorizeRefusesLowerEpoch/exact_lease` | N-epoch-lte weakens `==` to `<=`; the lower token authorizes past the epoch arm while the ahead vectors still refuse in the same run. |\n85|| Lease equality | `TestAuthorizeRefusesSameEpochLoser/standard` | N-lease-vector admits exactly the standard loser; the prefix-sharing loser still refuses. |\n86|| Lease equality, prefix confusion | `TestAuthorizeRefusesSameEpochLoser/prefix_sharing` | N-lease-prefix compares first UUID segments only; the prefix-sharing loser authorizes while the standard loser still refuses. |\n87|| Launch classification, input side | `TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesRemote/input` | N-launch-add-input parks input instead of refusing; the hard-refusal assertion fails. |\n88|| Launch classification, restore side | `TestAuthorizeParksAndRefusesRemote/restore` | N-launch-drop-restore refuses restore instead of parking; the park assertion fails. |\n89|| Capability seal | `TestBindRefusesForgedToken` | N-bind-seal admits exactly the field-assembled seal; the zero token still refuses. |\n90|| Provider operation enum | `TestBindRefusesUnknownOperation` | N-bind-op admits exactly the bogus operation; the projection mints and the negative fails by success. |\n91|| Terminate target grammar | `TestTerminateStaleRefusesMalformedTarget/lease_not_uuid` | N-term-presented admits exactly `zzz`; the termination authorizes and the negative fails by success. |\n92|| Terminate winner grammar | `TestTerminateStaleRefusesGarbageWinner/epoch_zero_lease` | N-term-winner admits exactly the epoch-zero `zzz` winner; the termination authorizes and the negative fails by success. |\n93|| Terminate winner presence | `TestTerminateStaleRefusesWithoutWinner/force` | N-term-absent admits exactly the forced winnerless call; the refusal degrades to the malformed-observation class. |\n94|| Terminate force confirmation | `TestTerminateStaleRefusesWithoutForce/diagnostics` | N-term-force admits exactly the unforced diagnosed call; the termination authorizes and the negative fails by success. |\n95|| Terminate diagnostics | `TestTerminateStaleRefusesWithoutDiagnostics/force` | N-term-diag admits exactly the undiagnosed forced call; the termination authorizes and the negative fails by success. |\n96|| Terminate session binding | `TestTerminateStaleRefusesForeignSession/prefix_sharing` | N-term-session admits exactly the prefix-sharing foreign target; the refusal degrades to the live-owner class. |\n97|| Terminate live-owner guard | `TestTerminateStaleRefusesLiveOwner/epoch_one` | N-term-live admits exactly the epoch-1 live owner; the epoch-2 owner still refuses. |\n98|| Seal construction census | `TestLeaseTokenConstructorCensus` | T-census-alias adds an alias-backdoor plant preserving `leaseSeal`; the census rejects it while the full suite runs. |\n99|\n100|Crash/idempotency matrix: the gates perform no durable writes, so\n101|there is no crash seam. `TestGatesPerformNoDurableWrites` hashes the\n102|repository tree, evaluates every entry (passing and failing) with\n103|`Bind` and `AuthorizeTerminateStale`, and requires byte-identical\n104|trees and identical verdicts across two runs.\n105|\n106|Refusal classes are proven registered, never invented:\n107|`TestGateRefusalsUseRegisteredCodes` constructs each sentinel through\n108|`internal/axerror` with its exact exit (`lease_conflict`, `not_owner`,\n109|`stale_owner` at 10; `invalid_arguments` at 2;\n110|`local_precondition_failed` at 3), and every park decision unwraps to\n111|its underlying Section 15 cause.\n112|\n113|## Bounds (not silent gaps)\n114|\n115|- No public CLI: 0 of 18 rows are delivered as an `ax` command. The\n116|  shared-library entries above are the deliverable; orchestration\n117|  leaves invoke them.\n118|- No takeover/fork/stop/resume transactions: lifecycle flows are\n119|  modeled as gate callers in `TestLifecycleCallersPassTheGate`; their\n120|  orchestration belongs to the owning leaves.\n121|- No terminal backend or provider plugin process: the gates own the\n122|  wrapper and provider-operation entry points only.\n123|- No `sessckpt` capture admission to reuse: no such package exists in\n124|  this tree, so `AuthorizeCheckpoint` is the capture admission and its\n125|  tests drive it directly.\n126|- No `resume`, `stop`, `materialize-commit`, or `native-store-plan`\n127|  provider binding: the wire triple is identical, but binding those\n128|  operations here without their callers would be an untestable claim.\n129|- No wall-clock lease expiry and no persisted grants: expiry retires\n130|  only the process-local authorization through the `sessrepo` owner;\n131|  the lease stays authoritative.\n132|- Clause 5.3#5 (`max_observed_epoch + 1`) is caller-side input: the\n133|  store mints head plus one, and the initiator's union maximum arrives\n134|  with the synced store the gate reads.\n135|- Precedence is decided and pinned: malformed calls die first, then\n136|  foreign sessions, then presence and verifiability, then the grant,\n137|  then direction, then the exact tuple match (`TestAuthorizePrecedence`).","final_result":true}}}
