\\\": \\\"ErrInvalidScalar is the internal/scalar refusal funnel for the common wire scalars Section 1.6 declares, but its CBOR decoder clauses, its UTF-16 ordering derivation clause and its wall-clock-ownership clause have no implementation, and no clause of Section 1.6 is enumerated against an acceptance case.\\\"\\ninternal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json:3418:      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Section 17.2 carries exactly one scanner-visible obligation, clause 17.2#1: a reader MAY retain an unknown event as inert history but MUST NOT derive state from it. That clause binds Session Event history, and Read classifies one completed CLI invocation rather than retaining any event, so this binding discharges none of Section 17.2's measured obligations. The four numbered reader rules the section states carry no RFC 2119 keyword and are therefore invisible to the clause scanner; three of them are implemented and tested here - Read and Decode settle the schema and major before any other member, the closed member set included, acceptsVersion implements the same-or-lower-minor rule, and an unknown namespaced extension survives a decode and re-encode byte for byte - while the unknown ownership/security enum rule is covered only for the closed CLI Result vocabularies, not for any lease or security enum, because no ownership implementation exists in this repository.\\\"\\ninternal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json:4436:      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Authorize with the lease store discharges 4 of the 22 Section 2.2 clauses (one winning owner, replica restraint, winning-epoch carriage, losing-event rejection); clauses 2.2#5 through 2.2#22 stay unimplemented here: the replication, secret, SQLite, materialization, tombstone, profile, capability, bridge, sync, continuation, readiness, and exclusion invariants plus the directory-merge preamble have no implementation in this ownership story.\\\",\\ninternal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json:4504:      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"The pinned section explicitly calls the predicates synthetic execution context and separates detailed DER, custody and runtime boundaries from policy witnesses. Upstream source publication ownership remains agent-session-manager-spec; TASK-260830-2x16gz owns consuming this evidence and proving real AX host admission.\\\"\\ninternal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json:4529:      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"The pinned section explicitly distinguishes the publication evaluator from runtime authority/durability obligations. Upstream source publication ownership remains agent-session-manager-spec; TASK-260830-1i7bqr owns product-level composed conformance using the shared resolver and lifecycle APIs.\\\"\\ninternal/traceability/traceability_test.go:150:\\t\\tmutate   func(*ownershipRegistry)\\ninternal/traceability/traceability_test.go:154:\\t\\t\\tname: \\\"one registered contract loses ownership\\\",\\ninternal/traceability/traceability_test.go:155:\\t\\t\\tmutate: func(registry *ownershipRegistry) {\\ninternal/traceability/traceability_test.go:156:\\t\\t\\t\\tgroup := ownershipGroupByKind(t, registry, ownershipContract)\\ninternal/traceability/traceability_test.go:162:\\t\\t\\tname: \\\"one nonempty normative section loses ownership\\\",\\ninternal/traceability/traceability_test.go:163:\\t\\t\\tmutate: func(registry *ownershipRegistry) {\\ninternal/traceability/traceability_test.go:164:\\t\\t\\t\\tgroup := ownershipGroupByKind(t, registry, ownershipNormativeSection)\\ninternal/traceability/traceability_test.go:170:\\t\\t\\tname: \\\"one exact catalog section binding loses ownership\\\",\\ninternal/traceability/traceability_test.go:171:\\t\\t\\tmutate: func(registry *ownershipRegistry) {\\ninternal/traceability/traceability_test.go:177:\\t\\t\\tname: \\\"one exact fixture loses ownership\\\",\\ninternal/traceability/traceability_test.go:178:\\t\\t\\tmutate: func(registry *ownershipRegistry) {\\ninternal/traceability/traceability_test.go:179:\\t\\t\\t\\tgroup := ownershipGroupByKind(t, registry, owne