{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5c1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2e-304f-7791-b344-a738da145935"},"sequence":315,"recorded_at":1780531400000625,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3f9b309c-9633-41a9-b30f-c2d9c31c28f3","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"3f9b309c-9633-41a9-b30f-c2d9c31c28f3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3f9b309c-9633-41a9-b30f-c2d9c31c28f3"},"call_id":"call_01a0ae2ee22977f181e796cc572e275e","text":"LOGBOOK.md:882:- NOTE: §7.1 has no ownership binding at all — the registry binds 7.2/7.3/7.4/7.5/7.A/7.8/7.9 to the placeholder `catalog.ForRelease` and never mentions 7.1. The deferral reason is accurate (`traceability.go:422` pins the projection to `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256`), but the section is now implemented and must be claimed before the Story closes.\nLOGBOOK.md:1256:- FINDING: reapplying the object-store Story onto trunk `010d114` produced eight conflict blocks. Seven were the expected shapes — the README tools row, the README acceptance-case sentence, `AcceptanceCases` in `traceability_test.go`, the two `acceptance_cases=` CLI strings, `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256`, and an add/add `LOGBOOK.md`. The eighth was not a conflict block at all: git auto-merged BOTH sides' `section:3.2` bindings into `ownership.v0.5.0.json` as two separate array entries, which `verifyOwnershipGroups` refuses at `traceability.go:404` as a `duplicate section_binding implementation owner`. A structural collision that presents as a clean text merge.\nLOGBOOK.md:1259:- DECISION: `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` was RECOMPUTED from the `traceability.go:286` refusal against the union-merged registry (`b5882b265b29d0c286c62a0263a6a38444d972434a5c5d42569efe6fc3af0b2c`), never copied. Base 29 + trunk 9 + accepted 5 = 43 acceptance cases, confirmed by `tracecheck` rather than asserted.\nLOGBOOK.md:1281:- DECISION: `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` was RECOMPUTED from the `traceability.go:286` refusal against the union-merged registry (`f126a4a00c64744586cc9d2bfc07e03a3923a93ee910970fe9183c9869759716`), never copied from either side. Copying trunk's value would have made the gate pass over a registry neither side reviewed.\nLOGBOOK.md:1391:- FINDING: the accepted revision-2 patch reapplied cleanly except `internal/traceability/traceability.go`, where trunk had independently repinned `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256`; resolved to the trunk value, then repinned to the recomputed projection digest `9f7737cb07f853012fcc9e2359981e20e9b65df622f9da7fa4935a2180cd04b0` reported by tracecheck.\nLOGBOOK.md:1412:- FINDING: registering new evidence tests in `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json` requires repinning `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` in `internal/traceability/traceability.go:42`; tracecheck fails closed on the projection digest until the repin is reviewed.\ninternal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go:558:\tconst assignment = `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 = \"`\ninternal/traceability/traceability.go:40:\t// reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 pins the semantic JSON projection. JSON\ninternal/traceability/traceability.go:43:\treviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 = \"94e589c880a263a61fe3e4e12ed836e076dd7e5bc074b6f6596de35231a53417\"\ninternal/traceability/traceability.go:437:\tif gotDigest != reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 {\ninternal/traceability/traceability.go:438:\t\treturn Report{}, fail(\"ownership registry projection digest %s differs from reviewed %s\", gotDigest, reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"search","outcome":"success"}}}
