{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c745","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2e-304f-7791-b344-a738da145935"},"sequence":509,"recorded_at":1780531400001013,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3f9b309c-9633-41a9-b30f-c2d9c31c28f3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3f9b309c-9633-41a9-b30f-c2d9c31c28f3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3f9b309c-9633-41a9-b30f-c2d9c31c28f3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae2f-57f5-78e3-9514-35b04b36fe2f"},"task_id":"01a0ae2f-57f5-78e3-9514-35b04b36fe2f","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae2f-57f5-78e3-9514-35b04b36fe2f","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-10-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"internal/fencing\\\\|Property suite\\\\|property-test\\\\|ownership.*reducer\\\\|Union-order\\\\|Clock non\\\" README.md | head -n 40; echo ===; grep -n \\\"Specification-to-Code Ownership Gate\\\" -A 10 README.md | head -n 30\",\n  \"description\": \"Check README fencing and ownership sections\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"1866:[`internal/fencing`](internal/fencing) gates every activation-class action on\\n1898:go test ./internal/fencing -count=1\\n1899:go test ./internal/fencing -cover -count=1\\n1906:python3 internal/fencing/testdata/mutate.py /absolute/path/to/new/evidence-dir\\n1917:[the task evidence map](internal/fencing/TRACEABILITY.md).\\n2823:[`internal/fencing`](internal/fencing), whose discharged clauses are the\\n2974:| `fencing` mutation harness | Run isolated fencing-gate narrowing mutants, one token-preserving census mutant, and three controls with real test-exit classification | `python3 internal/fencing/testdata/mutate.py /absolute/path/to/evidence-dir` | `mutants.json` and per-mutant logs under the supplied evidence directory; copied sources are restored and isolated |\\n===\\n391:[Specification-to-Code Ownership Gate](#specification-to-code-ownership-gate).\\n392-\\n393-## Provider Plugin Discovery and Trust\\n394-\\n395-[`internal/provider`](internal/provider) implements the Section 7.1 trusted\\n396-provider plugin host boundary: deterministic executable discovery, trust\\n397-recording, and substitution detection. `Discover` is the production entry\\n398-point. It enumerates candidates in the section's source order — configured\\n399-`providers.plugin_dirs` in listed order (entry names sorted bytewise within\\n400-each directory), then the six built-in adapters (`codex`, `claude`, `gemini`,\\n401-`muse`, `antigravity`, `pi`), then `PATH` only when `allow_path_plugins` is\\n--\\n518:arm, so a planted arm or a deleted branch reddens in either direction. This inventory is independent of the per-package refusal inventories in [`internal/provider`](internal/provider) above and [`internal/terminalbackend`](internal/terminalbackend) below (see [Specification-to-Code Ownership Gate](#specification-to-code-ownership-gate)): each package derives its own refusal arms from its own source in its own test file, and the three share no inventory code or table.\\n519-stdoutCap is pinned at MaxFrameBytes+2 in both directions, with a\\n520-maximal-frame-plus-junk probe through the production runner proving the\\n521-probe byte is load-bearing.\\n522-\\n523-## Safe Process and Filesystem Primitives\\n524-\\n525-[`internal/secprim`](internal/secprim) implements the shared safe\\n526-process and filesystem primitives of Sections 16.3, 16.4, and 16.7:\\n527-no-follow path handling, staging containment, structured argv,\\n528-environment allowlists, terminal control-string escaping, and secret\\n--\\n2679:## Specification-to-Code Ownership Gate\\n2680-\\n2681-[`internal/traceability`](internal/traceability) provides the read-only\\n2682-repository gate used by CI. Its reviewed\\n2683-[`ownership.v0.6.0.json`](internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json)\\n2684-registry independently enumerates implementation owners for all 63 current\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 2793,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 699,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
