{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c749","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2e-304f-7791-b344-a738da145935"},"sequence":511,"recorded_at":1780531400001017,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3f9b309c-9633-41a9-b30f-c2d9c31c28f3","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"3f9b309c-9633-41a9-b30f-c2d9c31c28f3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3f9b309c-9633-41a9-b30f-c2d9c31c28f3"},"call_id":"call_01a0ae2f47ac732994c762d91c5caba5","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-9-1\",\n  \"command\": \"python3 -c \\\"\\nimport json\\nreg=json.load(open('internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json'))\\nprint('acceptance_cases:', len(reg['acceptance_cases']))\\nfor ac in reg['acceptance_cases'][-15:]:\\n    print(ac['id'], '->', ac['production'])\\nprint()\\nprint('ownership groups:', len(reg['ownership']))\\nfor g in reg['ownership']:\\n    keys=','.join(g['keys'])\\n    if any(k in keys for k in ['2.2','5.3','13.6','13.7','13.8','13.9','13.10','17.2']):\\n        print(g['kind'], keys, '| prod:', g['production'], '| cov:', g.get('coverage'), '| ac:', g.get('acceptance_cases'))\\n        print('  gap:', (g.get('gap') or '')[:300])\\n        print('  clauses:', len(g.get('clauses',[])))\\n\\\"\",\n  \"description\": \"Summarize ownership registry bindings\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"acceptance_cases: 110\\ndirectory-node-scan -> {'path': 'internal/dirnode/scan.go', 'declaration': 'CheckScanRequest'}\\ndirectory-node-query -> {'path': 'internal/dirnode/query.go', 'declaration': 'DecodeQuery'}\\ndirectory-node-idempotency -> {'path': 'internal/dirnode/scan.go', 'declaration': 'CheckAndRecord'}\\nsource-pin-v060-exact -> {'path': 'internal/specpin/pin.go', 'declaration': 'CurrentV060'}\\nsource-pin-v060-refusal -> {'path': 'internal/specpin/pin.go', 'declaration': 'VerifyV060'}\\ncatalog-v060-exact -> {'path': 'internal/catalog/catalog.go', 'declaration': 'Current'}\\nlease-record-lifecycle -> {'path': 'internal/sessrepo/lease_store.go', 'declaration': 'CompareAndSwapLease'}\\nlease-fencing-revalidation -> {'path': 'internal/sessrepo/lease_store.go', 'declaration': 'VerifyFencingToken'}\\nlease-checkpoint-admission -> {'path': 'internal/sessquery/lease.go', 'declaration': 'winningLeaseFor'}\\nlease-divergent-preservation -> {'path': 'internal/sessrepo/sessrepo.go', 'declaration': 'AppendEvent'}\\nlease-union-resolution -> {'path': 'internal/sessstate/sessstate.go', 'declaration': 'Reduce'}\\nlease-fencing-gates -> {'path': 'internal/fencing/gate.go', 'declaration': 'Authorize'}\\nlease-fencing-park -> {'path': 'internal/fencing/gate.go', 'declaration': 'AuthorizeActivation'}\\nlease-terminate-stale -> {'path': 'internal/fencing/terminate.go', 'declaration': 'AuthorizeTerminateStale'}\\nlease-token-capability -> {'path': 'internal/fencing/token.go', 'declaration': 'Bind'}\\n\\nownership groups: 62\\nnormative_section catalog:10.8.5,catalog:11.2-11.3, 11.8-11.9,catalog:15.1-15.3,catalog:18.1,catalog:4.B-4.C,catalog:4.D,catalog:5.2, 13.14.5, 13.15,catalog:7.2, 7.5, 7.A,catalog:7.3-7.4,catalog:7.8,catalog:7.9,catalog:9.2 | prod: {'path': 'internal/cataloggen/generate.go', 'declaration': 'Generate'} | cov: None | ac: ['catalog-traceability-refusal', 'catalog-durable-recovery']\\n  gap: \\n  clauses: 0\\nsection_binding section:17.2 | prod: {'path': 'internal/cliresult/client.go', 'declaration': 'Read'} | cov: unevidenced | ac: ['cli-result-machine-reading', 'cli-result-identity-precedence', 'structured-error-identity-precedence', 'cli-result-historical-envelopes', 'structured-error-historical-envelopes', 'config-versioned-readers', 'config-current-writer', 'structured-error-common-data-model']\\n  gap: Section 17.2 carries exactly one scanner-visible obligation, clause 17.2#1: a reader MAY retain an unknown event as inert history but MUST NOT derive state from it. That clause binds Session Event history, and Read classifies one completed CLI invocation rather than retaining any event, so this bind\\n  clauses: 0\\nsection_binding section:5.3 | prod: {'path': 'internal/sessrepo/lease_store.go', 'declaration': 'CompareAndSwapLease'} | cov: partial | ac: ['lease-record-lifecycle', 'lease-fencing-revalidation', 'lease-checkpoint-admission', 'lease-divergent-preservation', 'lease-union-resolution', 'lease-fencing-gates', 'core-record-identity-validation']\\n  gap: CompareAndSwapLease with the fencing gates discharges 7 of the 8 Section 5.3 clauses; clause 5.3#5 (every new takeover lease MUST use max_observed_epoch + 1 from the initiator's union) stays unimplemented because the union maximum is caller-side input and no takeover flow exists in this repository y\\n  clauses: 7\\nsection_binding section:15.3 | prod: {'path': 'internal/axerror/registry.go', 'declaration': 'ExitCodeFor'} | cov: partial | ac: ['structured-error-code-exit-registry', 'structured-error-unknown-code-reader', 'structured-error-typed-details', 'cli-result-historical-envelopes', 'structured-error-exit-status-fan-in']\\n  gap: Clause 15.3#3 additionally forbids Structured Error from appearing as an RPC hello key or a TerminalBackend capability, and ExitCodeFor resolves a code-to-exit mapping rather than building either advertisement. No RPC hello frame is built anywhere in this repository, and the closed 16-capability adm\\n  clauses: 2\\nsection_binding section:2.2 | prod: {'path': 'internal/fencing/gate.go', 'declaration': 'Authorize'} | cov: sliver | ac: ['lease-fencing-gates', 'lease-fencing-park', 'lease-divergent-preservation', 'lease-union-resolution']\\n  gap: Authorize with the lease store discharges 4 of the 22 Section 2.2 clauses (one winning owner, replica restraint, winning-epoch carriage, losing-event rejection); clauses 2.2#5 through 2.2#22 stay unimplemented here: the replication, secret, SQLite, materialization, tombstone, profile, capability, br\\n  clauses: 4\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 4476,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1119,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
