{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c8a9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2e-304f-7791-b344-a738da145935"},"sequence":687,"recorded_at":1780531400001369,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3f9b309c-9633-41a9-b30f-c2d9c31c28f3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3f9b309c-9633-41a9-b30f-c2d9c31c28f3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3f9b309c-9633-41a9-b30f-c2d9c31c28f3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae30-013a-7d43-8d60-b127a08fde9b"},"task_id":"01a0ae30-013a-7d43-8d60-b127a08fde9b","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae30-013a-7d43-8d60-b127a08fde9b","chunk":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(1849 line(s) above)\n1850|behavioral test. The gate's own narrowing that admits only the simple\n1851|`kind := event.Type` copy is killed by the live PB control. Run this focused\n1852|composition with:\n1853|\n1854|```bash\n1855|go test ./internal/sessstate -count=1 -run '^TestCensusLiveEventOwnershipPlants$' -v\n1856|```\n1857|\n1858|The live test uses a temporary package copy and read-only dependency symlinks;\n1859|it restores its copied sources and never mutates the managed worktree. It runs\n1860|on the normal package suite and adds compiler/subprocess time. Task validation\n1861|logs and mutation artifacts are attached to `TASK-260830-1r9wrr`; scratch\n1862|outputs live under `.temp/TASK-260830-1r9wrr/`.\n1863|\n1864|## Provider and pane fencing gates\n1865|\n1866|[`internal/fencing`](internal/fencing) gates every activation-class action on\n1867|the winning lease and the exact fencing epoch (pinned v0.6.0 Sections 2.2,\n1868|5.3, and 13.6-13.10, the Section 4 terminal wrapper rule, and the Section 7.5\n1869|`LeaseToken`). `Observe` loads the winning lease through the `sessrepo` owner\n1870|and combines it with the caller's sync, handoff, grant, and clock facts;\n1871|`AuthorizeActivation`, `AuthorizeInput`, `AuthorizeMutation`,\n1872|`AuthorizeCheckpoint`, and `AuthorizeRestore` decide over that observation\n1873|through one core, and `AuthorizeTerminateStale` gates stale-process\n1874|termination. A passed gate mints a sealed `LeaseToken` that binds the exact\n1875|`{session_id, lease_epoch, lease_id}` triple to the `quiesce`, `capture`, and\n1876|`materialize` provider operations; a failed gate refuses with a Section 15\n1877|registered code and nothing else (`lease_conflict`, `not_owner`, `stale_owner`\n1878|at exit 10, `invalid_arguments` at exit 2, `local_precondition_failed` at\n1879|exit 3, proven by constructing each through `internal/axerror`). Launch-class\n1880|entries park instead of refusing when ownership is remote, ambiguous,\n1881|unverified, or absent, carrying the Section 5.2 `session.parked` vocabulary\n1882|(`remote_owner`, `stale_owner`, `restore_policy`, `failed_handoff`) with the\n1883|winning lease ID; every other entry refuses outright. Takeover, fork, stop,\n1884|and resume transactions are modeled as callers, not members: the gates own\n1885|their entry points only, and terminal backends and provider plugin processes\n1886|stay outside the package.\n1887|\n1888|The gates are pure over durable inputs: they perform no writes, hold no\n1889|cache, and read no clock except the caller-supplied reading, so there is no\n1890|crash seam and repeated evaluation decides identically. The sealed token has\n1891|no exported field or constructor — only the gate mints it — and an AST census\n1892|pins that boundary with comment/string controls plus an alias-backdoor plant\n1893|that preserves the searched-for token while changing the construction path.\n1894|\n1895|Run the focused tests and coverage with:\n1896|\n1897|```bash\n1898|go test ./internal/fencing -count=1\n1899|go test ./internal/fencing -cover -count=1\n1900|```\n1901|\n1902|Run the narrowing battery (30 narrowing mutants plus one token-preserving\n1903|census mutant and three controls) with:\n1904|\n1905|```bash\n1906|python3 internal/fencing/testdata/mutate.py /absolute/path/to/new/evidence-dir\n1907|```\n1908|\n1909|The harness copies the tree, applies each plant, runs the named behavioral\n1910|tests (the full suite for the census mutant), and writes per-mutant logs with\n1911|real exits to `mutants.json`; it restores its copied sources and never\n1912|mutates the managed worktree. Task validation logs and mutation artifacts are\n1913|attached to `TASK-260830-3g12yp`; scratch outputs live under\n1914|`.temp/TASK-260830-3g12yp/`. The package adds no `ax` command, no `doctor`\n1915|result, and no runtime capability claim; the clause-to-test matrix with its\n1916|stated bounds lives in\n1917|[the task evidence map](internal/fencing/TRACEABILITY.md).\n1918|\n1919|## Session selector, read summaries, and selection plans\n1920|\n1921|`internal/sessquery` is the single shared selector API over the persisted\n1922|session repositories and the accepted state projector. It implements the\n1923|v0.6.0 selector contract (§14.7/§14.7.1, refining §2.3) with shared\n1924|SelectionPlan construction and revalidation (§14.7.2):\n1925|\n1926|- Literal grammar: split at the first `@` only. The key is a NAME, a bare\n1927|  UUID (name-first precedence kept), or `id:UUID` (bypasses names for the\n1928|  durable union identity). The source is empty (bare §2.3 tiers), `local`,\n1929|  `peer:ALIAS` (the entire remaining suffix, literal — spaces, `@`,\n1930|  Unicode, and `%` included), or `id:HOST_UUID`. No joining, aliasing,\n1931|  percent-decoding, Unicode normalization, trimming, or alias folding.\n1932|- Exact source mappings: effective configuration (local host, peer\n1933|  alias/host mappings, allowlist) is validated first, including exact\n1934|  alias and host-ID uniqueness; duplicates are `invalid_config`.\n1935|  Explicit unknown aliases/hosts are `selector_source_not_found`; known\n1936|  but disallowed peers are `peer_not_allowlisted`. Remote read failures\n1937|  are `selector_source_read_failed` with the cause preserved; local I/O\n1938|  keeps its repository error; malformed authority is `integrity_failure`.\n1939|- No explicit-source fallback: a qualified key resolves in its one\n1940|  source only. Tier, collision, and tombstone semantics follow §14.7.1:\n1941|  exact live name then UUID-shaped name within the source, replicated\n1942|  copies deduplicate only on agreeing record digests (else\n1943|  `integrity_failure`), distinct colliding names refuse with\n1944|  `name_ambiguous`, and tombstoned entries stay excluded on\n1945|  authoritative tombstone evidence while failed reads never count as it.\n1946|- Immutable plans: `Reader.BuildPlan` binds all sixteen §14.7.2\n1947|  members — the literal selector, session and validated record digest,\n1948|  source host (always a UUIDv7; a local selection without a known local\n1949|  host refuses `invalid_config`) and exact alias, index and\n1950|  configuration digests, the validated winning `urn:ax:schema:lease`\n1951|  Lease Record digest with its epoch, lease ID, and holder from that\n1952|  same record (admitted through the canonicaljson owner from\n1953|  `Reader.LeaseRecords`, greatest (epoch, lease_id) winner with a\n1954|  fully validated succession: the predecessor ancestry chains by\n1955|  epoch plus one to an epoch-1 null-predecessor root, and every\n1956|  lease in that winning ancestry above epoch 1 references an\n1957|  admitted `urn:ax:schema:checkpoint` Checkpoint Record from\n1958|  `Reader.CheckpointRecords` for its session and predecessor lease,\n1959|  each created by the owning lease holder, each carrying the\n1960|  persistence variant the referenced Session Record kind selects\n1961|  (direct only provider-manifest, task_board only task-board-bundle;\n1962|  §5.4), and each resolving every event head to a chained event for\n1963|  its session at or before its bound lease in the winning source\n1964|  chain (historical heads admissible, never required to equal the\n1965|  current tail; missing, cross-session, losing-lease, and later-lease\n1966|  heads refuse), and each admitting its Section 2.4 profile authority\n1967|  over the same closure (first launch carries the creation pair,\n1968|  later launches the newest authoritative change at or before them,\n1969|  resumes their referenced checkpoint's pair, forks the new record\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
