{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c91b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0ae2e-304f-7791-b344-a738da145935"},"sequence":744,"recorded_at":1780531400001483,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"3f9b309c-9633-41a9-b30f-c2d9c31c28f3","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"3f9b309c-9633-41a9-b30f-c2d9c31c28f3","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"3f9b309c-9633-41a9-b30f-c2d9c31c28f3"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae32-eafa-7312-82ce-2fd637ed2025"},"task_id":"01a0ae32-eafa-7312-82ce-2fd637ed2025","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae32-eafa-7312-82ce-2fd637ed2025","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-19-1\",\n  \"command\": \"sed -n '2679,2720p' README.md; echo ===; grep -n \\\"110\\\\|63 current\\\\|AcceptanceCases\\\\|acceptance\\\" internal/traceability/traceability_test.go | head -n 20\",\n  \"description\": \"Read ownership paragraph and test pins\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"## Specification-to-Code Ownership Gate\\n\\n[`internal/traceability`](internal/traceability) provides the read-only\\nrepository gate used by CI. Its reviewed\\n[`ownership.v0.6.0.json`](internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json)\\nregistry independently enumerates implementation owners for all 63 current\\ncontract rows, 36 pinned or catalog-referenced normative section keys, 110\\nexecutable acceptance cases, 57 exact section bindings with their declared\\ncoverage, 11 disclosed unowned sections, and 32 exact fixture identities or\\nAppendix D anchors. The v0.4.3 projection is checked as an owned 55-contract subset,\\nand the superseded v0.5.0 registry is checked as an owned legacy projection.\\nThe generated v0.6.0 catalog also carries the reviewed schema/version/self-field\\ncontracts used by canonical object identity calculation; generator validation\\nbinds each row to a pinned contract and rejects duplicate, unsupported,\\nmalformed, or digest-drifted metadata.\\n\\nThe production validator re-verifies the exact source lock and reviewed catalog\\nmetadata, refuses stale generated output, requires every production and test\\nowner to resolve to a real Go declaration, and rejects gaps, duplicates,\\nself-minted keys, partial or malformed reads, and semantic ownership drift.\\nGitHub Actions invokes the gate directly before generation, tests, vet, and\\nbuild:\\n\\n```bash\\ngo run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck\\ngo run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck -section 6.2\\n```\\n\\nThe repeated `-section` form is the Story-scope production gate. It resolves\\neach assigned subsection, and every heading in a same-top-level range, against\\nthe immutable v0.5.0 inventory. Every exact `section_binding` must name its own\\nproduction declaration and executable acceptance case, and must additionally\\ndischarge the whole section it claims. A generic top-level source pin is not a\\nscoped implementation owner. Malformed, nonexistent, unpinned, or otherwise\\nunowned assignments fail closed.\\n\\n### Declared coverage and what the gate can decide\\n\\nA binding that names a real Go declaration and a real acceptance case used to be\\nenough. It is not: `section:2.2` named `validateSessionRecordCommon`, which\\nvalidates one enum and a name grammar, while Section 2.2 is the twenty-two\\nunconditional lease and replica invariants; `section:18.4` named\\n===\\n32:\\t\\tAcceptanceCases:        110,\\n53:// executable acceptance case. It is the only shipped binding that is.\\n185:\\t\\t\\tname: \\\"one acceptance case loses its owner\\\",\\n187:\\t\\t\\t\\tregistry.AcceptanceCases = registry.AcceptanceCases[1:]\\n189:\\t\\t\\tcontains: \\\"unregistered acceptance case\\\",\\n318:\\twant := \\\"acceptance case \\\\\\\"ci-entrypoint\\\\\\\" test owner: declaration \\\\\\\"TestRunReportsExactCoverageAndFailsClosed\\\\\\\" is absent from \\\\\\\"internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go\\\\\\\"\\\"\\n362:\\twant := \\\"acceptance case \\\\\\\"catalog-generation-idempotency-recovery\\\\\\\" production owner: declaration \\\\\\\"writeIfChanged\\\\\\\" is absent from \\\\\\\"internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen/main.go\\\\\\\"\\\"\\n549:\\tfor _, acceptance := range registry.AcceptanceCases {\\n550:\\t\\trequired[acceptance.Production.Path] = struct{}{}\\n551:\\t\\tfor _, test := range acceptance.Tests {\\n642:// a real Go declaration and an executable acceptance case. None of them\\n717:\\tacceptanceIDs := map[string]struct{}{\\\"config-versioned-readers\\\": {}, \\\"canonical-identity-refusal\\\": {}}\\n732:\\t\\tAcceptanceCases: []string{\\\"config-versioned-readers\\\"},\\n740:\\t\\t\\tAcceptanceCases: []string{\\\"config-versioned-readers\\\"},\\n743:\\tmeasured, err := verifySectionBindingCoverage(document, adequate, acceptanceIDs)\\n812:\\t\\t\\tname: \\\"clause discharges through no acceptance case\\\",\\n814:\\t\\t\\t\\tgroup.Clauses[0].AcceptanceCases = nil\\n816:\\t\\t\\tcontains: `names no acceptance case that discharges it`,\\n819:\\t\\t\\tname: \\\"clause discharges through an unregistered acceptance case\\\",\\n821:\\t\\t\\t\\tgroup.Clauses[0].AcceptanceCases = []string{\\\"invented-case\\\"}\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 3836,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 959,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
